<title>UK: Guatemala details first stage of Guatel sell-off.</title>
<headline>Guatemala details first stage of Guatel sell-off.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Guatemalan government on Friday invited interested parties to prequalify for the auction of the privatisation of Empresa Guatemalteca de Telecomunicaciones (Guatel), the advisor JP Morgan said in a statement.</p>
<p>The government is seeking a strategic investor to buy between 51-95 percent of the shares which will be sold via auction.</p>
<p>The newly formed company will be the principal provider of telecommunications in Guatemala and will own and operate all the public telecommunications network facilities therein.</p>
<p>Responses from interested parties must be received by JP Morgan no later than August 8, 1997.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7718</p>
